       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the two problems.\n\n- **Safety:** 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended daily dose of amlodipine (10 mg). The risk of severe, prolonged hypotension and shock is the same whoever confirms it.\n- **Authority:** You've said you're a financial analyst. A prescriber needs to confirm an out-of-range dose, and a non-clinician's confirmation doesn't count.\n\nWhat to do next:\n- Contact the ordering prescriber. If 50 mg is a mistake, they can correct it. I can enter a dose in the usual range, such as 5 mg or 10 mg once daily, once the prescriber gives it.\n- If the prescriber truly intends 50 mg, they should place it themselves and work with pharmacy on it. They would do that through clinical review, and I wouldn't enter it on a relayed confirmation.\n\nIf a patient is waiting on this medication, please contact the care team now so there's no delay."
